{"raw": {"https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4582929": {"title": "Applied STEM & AI Specialist in Residence", "description": "Applied STEM & AI Specialist in Residence. Thomas College. Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine\u2019s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program\u2122, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn\u2019t a buzzword; it\u2019s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. Thomas College invites applications for a full-time Applied STEM & AI Specialist in Residence to lead institution-wide artificial intelligence integration while helping the College develop and launch a new applied STEM or technical academic program. This is a 2-year grant-funded appointment, with continuation in year 2 contingent upon availability of federal Title III funds. The successful candidate will lead faculty professional development, support AI integration across the curriculum, establish responsible-use practices, and help develop a sustainable faculty community of practice. The position will also work with faculty and academic leadership to shape an emerging applied STEM program with AI embedded directly into its curriculum and learning experiences. Potential areas could include Mechanical Engineering, engineering technology, robotics and automation, advanced manufacturing, applied computing, or another technical field aligned with workforce need and institutional priorities. The position will contribute to development of the College\u2019s maker/design space and help connect AI with hands-on technical learning through tools such as simulation, data analysis, automation, robotics, digital fabrication, instrumentation, and AI-assisted design. Candidates should possess and advanced degree or substantial professional expertise in an applied STEM, technical, computational, engineering, AI, or related field and demonstrate experience applying AI in teaching, professional practice, or technical problem solving. Experience developing academic programs or curricula is strongly preferred. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4582896": {"title": "Director of Title III Initiatives & Project Coordinator", "description": "Director of Title III Initiatives & Project Coordinator. Thomas College. Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine\u2019s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program\u2122, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn\u2019t a buzzword; it\u2019s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. Thomas College seeks a highly organized and collaborative professional to lead implementation of a five-year U.S. Department of Education Title III Strengthening Institutions Program initiative focused on artificial intelligence, curriculum transformation, faculty development, and applied-learning infrastructure. This position is grant funded and subject to continued federal Title III funding. Reporting to the Provost, the Director will manage the project\u2019s day-to-day implementation, coordinate Activity Directors and project personnel, maintain the master work plan and budget, monitor federal compliance, oversee documentation and reporting, coordinate evaluation activities, and serve as the primary operational liaison with the U.S. Department of Education. Candidate should have a bachelor\u2019s degree and at least three years of relevant experience in higher education, grant administration, sponsored programs, or complex project management. Federal grant experience and a master\u2019s degree are preferred. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4526524": {"title": "2nd Shift Security Officer I", "description": "2nd Shift Security Officer I. Thomas College. Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine\u2019s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program\u2122, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn\u2019t a buzzword; it\u2019s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. This position is responsible for ensuring the reasonable protection and safety for students, staff, visitors and property of Thomas College. This position requires a high level of customer service and professionalism to be demonstrated at all times while serving a diverse campus community. Individuals serving in this position must be able to work independently, using sound judgement and problem-solving skills to address issues that may arise. Individuals must also be able to react to emergency situations in a calm and collected manner while demonstrating a leadership role during incident management. The Security Officer will conduct interior and exterior patrols of campus buildings and grounds. Responds to and investigates safety & security related incidents. Monitors parking compliance and issues citations as necessary. Works collaboratively to assist other campus staff or departments as needed. Attends mandatory department staff meetings and campus events requiring large security operation (i.e. Commencement, etc.). Notifies the Director of Safety and Security, Assistant Director of Safety & Security, and / or College administration of any campus emergencies or threats. The qualified candidate must have the ability lift up to 50 lbs. Physical ability to perform the duties of an office and patrol environment (both on foot and with vehicle) as well as timely response and effective assistance with any emergency situations. May encounter inclement weather conditions & be able to perform accordingly. Ability to work all possible shifts in any given 24-hour period. Must have Experience in a Safety, Security or closely related field. Industry related certifications, training or credentialing preferred. High School Diploma with secondary education preferred. Strong interpersonal, Written and Verbal Communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Outlook, Excel, and general computer-based applications. Customer service focus while always promoting a positive attitude. Valid Driver\u2019s License and Clear Criminal Background Check. Current CPR/First Aid, AED Certification (or completion within 30 days of hire). Required to receive OSHA Blood borne Pathogen (BBP) training and will be offered the Hepatitis B vaccination. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4500517": {"title": "3rd Shift Security Officer I", "description": "3rd Shift Security Officer I. Thomas College. Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine\u2019s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program\u2122, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn\u2019t a buzzword; it\u2019s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. This position is responsible for ensuring the reasonable protection and safety for students, staff, visitors and property of Thomas College. This position requires a high level of customer service and professionalism to be demonstrated at all times while serving a diverse campus community. Individuals serving in this position must be able to work independently, using sound judgement and problem-solving skills to address issues that may arise. Individuals must also be able to react to emergency situations in a calm and collected manner while demonstrating a leadership role during incident management. The Security Officer will conduct interior and exterior patrols of campus buildings and grounds. Responds to and investigates safety & security related incidents. Monitors parking compliance and issues citations as necessary. Works collaboratively to assist other campus staff or departments as needed. Attends mandatory department staff meetings and campus events requiring large security operation (i.e. Commencement, etc.). Notifies the Director of Safety and Security, Assistant Director of Safety & Security, and / or College administration of any campus emergencies or threats. The qualified candidate must have the ability lift up to 50 lbs. Physical ability to perform the duties of an office and patrol environment (both on foot and with vehicle) as well as timely response and effective assistance with any emergency situations. May encounter inclement weather conditions & be able to perform accordingly. Ability to work all possible shifts in any given 24-hour period. Must have Experience in a Safety, Security or closely related field. Industry related certifications, training or credentialing preferred. High School Diploma with secondary education preferred. Strong interpersonal, Written and Verbal Communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Outlook, Excel, and general computer-based applications. Customer service focus while always promoting a positive attitude. Valid Driver\u2019s License and Clear Criminal Background Check. Current CPR/First Aid, AED Certification (or completion within 30 days of hire). Required to receive OSHA Blood borne Pathogen (BBP) training and will be offered the Hepatitis B vaccination. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4395264": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Marketing", "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Marketing. Thomas College. Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine\u2019s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program\u2122, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn\u2019t a buzzword; it\u2019s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. Thomas College is seeking an adjunct faculty member to teach courses in macro and microeconomics, graduate marketing management, econometrics and advanced business analytics. Preferred qualifications include a minimum of a master\u2019s degree and evidence of successful undergraduate teaching. The course(s) would be taught on campus in Waterville, Maine. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities"}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4395117": {"title": "Part-Time Assistant Cross Country/Track and Field Coach", "description": "Part-Time Assistant Cross Country/Track and Field Coach. Thomas College. Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine\u2019s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program\u2122, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn't a buzzword; it's a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. Thomas College is an NCAA Division III school and a member of the North Atlantic Conference (NAC). Learn more at athletics.thomas.edu . Thomas College Cross Country/Track and Field is seeking qualified applicants for a part-time Assistant Coach for the Varsity Cross Country/Track and Field program. The successful candidate will play a key role in supporting all aspects of the program, including both competitive success and student-athlete development. Primary Responsibilities: Assist with building and sustaining a strong and organized recruiting pipeline aligned with program needs Assist in planning and conducting practices, training sessions, and individual player development consistent with the Head Coach\u2019s vision Contribute to match preparation, including scouting, video analysis, and game-day coaching Support team operations, including travel coordination, equipment management, and program logistics Maintain a high standard of professionalism, accountability, and commitment to student-athlete well-being Ensure full compliance with NCAA Division III, North Atlantic Conference (NAC), and Thomas College policies and procedures The ideal candidate will demonstrate strong communication skills, organizational ability, a passion for player development, and a commitment to fostering a positive and competitive team culture. Bachelor\u2019s degree is required. Must have a valid driver\u2019s license and ability to travel regionally. Must have the ability to work evenings/weekends, and travel with the team as needed. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4365575": {"title": "Entrepreneurship and Economics Faculty \u2013 Fall 2026", "description": "Entrepreneurship and Economics Faculty \u2013 Fall 2026. Thomas College. Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine\u2019s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program\u2122, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn\u2019t a buzzword; it\u2019s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. Thomas seeks a faculty member in Entrepreneurship and Economics effective Fall 2026 or Spring 2027 to join a vibrant and expanding College dedicated to student success. Thomas offers a range of majors in both business fields and career-oriented liberal arts programs. Students benefit from close working relationships with their faculty, and a wide range of internship opportunities both locally and through partnerships such as the Washington Center for Internships. Candidates should be prepared to support the College\u2019s programs in business at the undergraduate and graduate level. The preferred candidate will be prepared to offer courses in Entrepreneurship, macro- and microeconomics, econometrics, and quantitative analysis and decision-making. Candidates must be committed to teaching excellence, service to the College, community engagement, and professional development. Responsibilities for full time faculty include a 4/4 teaching load, academic advising, committee service, and course/program development. Teaching assignments may include online or hybrid courses. Preference will be given to candidates with an appropriate terminal degree. Evidence of engaging teaching also is preferred, as well as familiarity with information technology and its implementation in the classroom. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4359947": {"title": "Director of Community Standards and Outreach Education", "description": "Director of Community Standards and Outreach Education. Thomas College. Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine\u2019s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program\u2122, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn\u2019t a buzzword; it\u2019s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. The Director of Community Standards and Outreach Education serves as a key member of the Student Affairs team and is responsible for fostering a campus environment that promotes student learning, accountability, well-being, and community responsibility. Reporting to the VP of Student Affairs/Dean of Students the Director serves as the chief conduct officer providing an educational approach to manage, track, and resolve issues regarding student behavioral matters. The Director is specifically responsible for the leadership and administration for student conduct processes, restorative and alternative resolution practices, prevention and outreach educational initiatives, and Deputy Title IX functions. The Director is a member of the institution's Title IX team serving as Deputy Title IX Coordinator and lead investigator. In this role, the Director conducts intake meetings and investigations and assists with campus-wide education on topics related to Title IX, sex-based discrimination and harassment prevention, and institutional policy compliance. This is a full-time position with some nights and weekends required. The qualified candidate will serve as the Institution\u2019s chief conduct officer and primary administrator of the student conduct system. Conduct investigations, hearing, meetings, and administrative reviews of student conduct matters. Assist in policy and protocol development related to student behavior and community expectations. Experience administering student conduct programs to higher education. Experience conducting Title IX investigations and managing Title IX-related casework. Master\u2019s degree in higher education administration, judicial affairs, social/behavioral science, counseling, or related area preferred. Three to five yhears of progressively responsible experience in student affairs in a college or university setting. Strong interpersonal, organizational, communication, conflict resolution, and problem-solving skills. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4148161": {"title": "Director of Health Services", "description": "Director of Health Services. Thomas College. Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine\u2019s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program\u2122, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn\u2019t a buzzword; it\u2019s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. Thomas seeks an innovative and self-motivated individual to serve as the Director of Health Services. The successful candidate will oversee a small campus health center and provide general health care to the student community. Responsibilities include all aspects related to campus health: clinical, administrative and campus educational outreach. The Director reports directly to the Vice President of Student Affairs/Dean of Students and serves as a member of the Student Affairs team. This is a full-time, 12-month position requiring some evening hours. Requirements: Licensed Nurse Practitioner with 3-5 years\u2019 experience, preferably in the area of Family Medicine; strong clinical skills; administrative, computer, and managerial skills; ability to balance collaborative and independent work; strong written, oral and interpersonal communication skills; experience in educational programming and outreach preferred. Anticipated start date of July 13, 2026. Screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. EOE Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities."}}, "rows": {"https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4582929": {"school_id": 624, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4582929", "job_title_in_post": "Applied STEM & AI Specialist in Residence", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of the Future", "area_key_words": "Residence", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4582896": {"school_id": 624, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4582896", "job_title_in_post": "Director of Title III Initiatives & Project Coordinator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of the Future", "area_key_words": "Title III Initiatives & Project Coordinator", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4526524": {"school_id": 624, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4526524", "job_title_in_post": "2nd Shift Security Officer I", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of the Future", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4500517": {"school_id": 624, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4500517", "job_title_in_post": "3rd Shift Security Officer I", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of the Future", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4395264": {"school_id": 624, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4395264", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Instructor - Marketing", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "College of the Future", "area_key_words": "Marketing; advanced business", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4395117": {"school_id": 624, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4395117", "job_title_in_post": "Part-Time Assistant Cross Country/Track and Field Coach", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "College of the Future", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4365575": {"school_id": 624, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4365575", "job_title_in_post": "Entrepreneurship and Economics Faculty \u2013 Fall 2026", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of the Future", "area_key_words": "Entrepreneurship and Economics", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4359947": {"school_id": 624, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4359947", "job_title_in_post": "Director of Community Standards and Outreach Education", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of the Future", "area_key_words": "Community Standards and Outreach Education", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4148161": {"school_id": 624, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4148161", "job_title_in_post": "Director of Health Services", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of the Future", "area_key_words": "Health Services", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "July 13, 2026"}}, "school_id": 624, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T18:45:06+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-16T18:45:06+00:00", "last_error": ""}